"""[s3-chain] app.py half of the System 3 exchange handoff
(docs/system3-exchange-handoff-2026-09-28.md, steps 1-5).

  dj-speak-replies            dj_speak airs the admitted chapter's replies from its
                              shelf entry (pause/transport -> the rest is owed).
  prepared-shelf              _s3_prepare_line_chapter's one attempt becomes the
                              durable prepared shelf (data/system3_chapter_shelf.json):
                              pending -> prepared -> airing -> aired | partial | expired,
                              retries with backoff, a keeper task, replies checked
                              (stock / own direction / answers nothing said), the
                              whole exchange measured and fitted to its entry.
  microphone-admission        _dj_speak_floorless: admission from the shelf, or the
                              line WAITS (never a one-line fragment); a road whose
                              graph is off airs its line alone.
  chapter-rows-wait-for-the-box   a chapter row is never held for a later replay.
  round-chunk-names-its-turn  speak_turns' per-turn road passes the round's turn
                              stamp, so a chunk never plans a line node / chapter.
  produced-spot-*             floor wrapper, shelf admission, sid, missed opener,
                              the box ack restored under `if box_played`, replies.
  music-spot-*                the music-bed spot: floor wrapper, admission, replies.
  page-*                      the page from upstairs: floor wrapper, admission (its
                              split parts re-stamped onto the chapter), sid, and the
                              studio answers with the chapter instead of a second
                              dj_banter conversation (kept when no chapter applies).

Anchors cut from HEAD 617abbc, each unique; none lies inside another tool's
stored text (static ast scan of tools/*.py). --check exits 0 ready / 2 applied /
1 anchors missing; --apply is idempotent, asserts every anchor, writes LF
atomically. Apply AFTER tools/system3_chain_runtime_patch.py (the app half calls
system3_line_chapter_state through globals().get, so either order runs).
TARGET: app.py
"""
